{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_yxmm75odtnt63nxe4bnbikmm5xvrbic7g6zktsj3l3mcn6xy2mzq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_019FtUuqYiVD8iEM1uoDadCQ","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-1bfdsY/translated_rust/CONFIGS.md","old_string":"## Status\n\nAll 20 rows are implemented in `tests/differential.rs` (function names\n`row01_…` … `row20_…`) and pass under every feature combination listed above.","new_string":"## Status\n\nAll 20 rows are implemented in `tests/differential.rs` and pass under every\nfeature combination listed above (and additionally under `--release`).\n\n| row | test in `tests/differential.rs` | status |\n|-----|----------------------------------|--------|\n| 1 | `row01_loop_never_entered` | [x] |\n| 2 | `row02_x_zero_small_y` | [x] |\n| 3 | `row03_x_negative_y_positive` | [x] |\n| 4 | `row04_y_zero_small_x` | [x] |\n| 5 | `row05_y_zero_large_x` | [x] |\n| 6 | `row06_special_case_x1_y4` | [x] |\n| 7 | `row07_x1_y_not_4` | [x] |\n| 8 | `row08_x_not_1_y4` | [x] |\n| 9 | `row09_back_edge_boundary_x2` | [x] |\n| 10 | `row10_back_edge_boundary_x3` | [x] |\n| 11 | `row11_back_edge_flip_x4` | [x] |\n| 12 | `row12_mixed_back_edge` | [x] |\n| 13 | `row13_exhaustive_small_grid` | [x] |\n| 14 | `row14_random_small` | [x] |\n| 15 | `row15_random_medium` | [x] |\n| 16 | `row16_asymmetric_shapes` | [x] |\n| 17 | `row17_large_scale` | [x] |\n| 18 | `row18_sequencing_and_interleaving` | [x] |\n| 19 | `row19_extremes_bounded` | [x] |\n| 20 | `row20_multi_mib_output` | [x] |\n\nRoughly 5 800 distinct `(x, y)` configurations are compared per run, each with\nboth libraries invoked through their `.so` export.\n\n## How the comparison works\n\n`driver` is `void`-returning and communicates only through `stdout`, so the\nobservable output is the byte stream on fd 1 **plus** the process termination\nstatus. `tests/common/mod.rs` performs every call in a forked child whose fd 1\nis a temporary file, then compares the bytes *and* the raw `waitpid` status of\nthe C child against the Rust child. (A forked child is required: libtest keeps\nwriting its own progress lines to fd 1 from other threads, which would\ncontaminate an in-process redirect.)\n\nNon-terminating inputs (`x > 0 && y < 0`, `x` near `INT_MAX`) are compared as a\nbyte-capped prefix produced in a child that is `SIGKILL`ed once a full window\nhas been read — see `ERRORS.md` rows 14/15.\n\n## Reproducing\n\n```sh\n./check_all.sh                     # every feature combination, symbols + tests\ncargo build --offline              # NOTE: `cargo test` does not rebuild a cdylib\ncargo test  --offline              # the harness refuses to run on a stale .so\n```\n\nThe suite was validated by mutation testing: 8 independent mutations of\n`src/lib.rs` (`y == 4`→`y == 5`, `x < 3`→`x <= 3`, `y == 0`→`y <= 0`,\n`x > 0`→`x >= 0`, `||`→`&&`, `goto label2`→`goto label1`, `x--`→`x -= 2`,\n`\"loop\\n\"`→`\"Loop\\n\"`) were each detected by at least one failing test."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2622,"cache_read_input_tokens":104664,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2622,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eeb44132-fb7e-4437-9dd9-10fc85cd1842","uuid":"20e0e4be-4970-4dee-a1a8-0aedf25d6133","timestamp":"2026-08-18T04:04:16.779Z"}
