{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Ptv1QoGq9qWUt4EoZg6GgA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# CONFIGS.md — Phase A: configuration surface table (valid inputs)\n2\t\n3\tDerived mechanically from the C source, not from assumptions.\n4\t\n5\t## Build-time configuration\n6\t\n7\t| source | knobs found | conclusion |\n8\t|--------|-------------|------------|\n9\t| `Cargo.toml` | no `[features]` table at all (`grep -n feature Cargo.toml src/` → no matches) | exactly **one** build configuration |\n10\t| `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` | no `option()`, no `if()`, no `add_definitions`, no `target_compile_definitions` | one C build configuration |\n11\t| `c_src/*.c/h` | only `#ifndef DRIVER_H_` include guard — no conditional compilation | no `#ifdef` variants |\n12\t\n13\t**Feature combinations (all of them):**\n14\t\n15\t| # | cargo invocation | meaning |\n16\t|---|------------------|---------|\n17\t| 1 | `cargo <cmd> --no-default-features` | the empty feature set (identical to the default, since no features exist) |\n18\t| 2 | `cargo <cmd>` (default) | same as #1 |\n19\t| 3 | `cargo <cmd> --all-features` | same as #1 |\n20\t\n21\tAll three are the *same* configuration; `check_all.sh` runs check + build +\n22\tsymbol-diff + the full test suite for each of them anyway.\n23\t\n24\t## Runtime configuration axes (from the C branches)\n25\t\n26\tPublic API (`c_src/include/driver.h`) is a single, lowest-level entry point —\n27\tthere is no wrapper/convenience layer, so \"driving it like a real consumer\"\n28\tmeans calling `driver(x, y)` directly:\n29\t\n30\t```c\n31\tvoid driver(int x, int y);\n32\t```\n33\t\n34\tAxes = every condition the C code branches on (`driver.c`):\n35\t\n36\t| axis | source line | distinct states |\n37\t|------|-------------|-----------------|\n38\t| A: loop guard | `30: while (x > 0 \\|\\| y > 0)` | `x>0&&y>0`, `x>0&&y<=0`, `x<=0&&y>0`, `x<=0&&y<=0` |\n39\t| B: special case | `33: if (x == 1 && y == 4)` | true; false via `x!=1`; false via `y!=4` |\n40\t| C: `label1` guard | `38: if (x > 0)` | `x>0`, `x==0`, `x<0` |\n41\t| D: `label2` guard | `44: if (y == 0)` | `y==0` (on entry), `y==0` (reached mid-body), `y!=0` |\n42\t| E: back-edge | `49: if (x < 3)` | `x<3` (backward `goto label1`, **no** `while` re-test), `x>=3` (`while` re-test ⇒ extra `loop\\n`) |\n43\t| F: value shape | — | `0`, `1`, `2`, `3`, `4`, small, medium, large, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`, negatives |\n44\t| G: sequencing | — | repeated / interleaved invocations (checks for hidden state) |\n45\t| H: output volume | — | small (< stdio buffer) vs. multi-MiB (forces many `stdout` flushes) |\n46\t\n47\tRows below are the cross product of A–H pruned to the combinations the C code\n48\tactually distinguishes. Each row is exercised with **many randomized inputs**\n49\t(seeded LCG, fixed seed `0x2545F4914F6CDD1D`) wherever a range is involved, and\n50\tcompared byte-for-byte between the C `.so` and the Rust `.so`.\n51\t\n52\t`x > 0 && y < 0` is *excluded* from the valid-input rows: it makes the C library\n53\trun ≈2^31 iterations and hit signed-overflow UB (see `ERRORS.md` rows 14/15); it\n54\tis covered there by a byte-capped prefix comparison instead.\n55\t\n56\t| #  | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n57\t|----|----------------|-------------------------------------------|-----|\n58\t| 1  | `driver` | A=`x<=0&&y<=0`: randomized `x,y ∈ [INT_MIN, 0]` — loop never entered | [x] |\n59\t| 2  | `driver` | A=`x<=0&&y>0`, C=`x==0`: `x=0`, randomized `y ∈ [1,8]` — `label1` skipped, only the back-edge path runs | [x] |\n60\t| 3  | `driver` | A=`x<=0&&y>0`, C=`x<0` incl. `INT_MIN`: randomized `y ∈ [1,64]` | [x] |\n61\t| 4  | `driver` | A=`x>0&&y<=0`, D=`y==0` on entry, E=`x<3`: `x ∈ {1,2}`, `y=0` | [x] |\n62\t| 5  | `driver` | A=`x>0&&y<=0`, D=`y==0`, E=`x>=3`: randomized `x ∈ [3,40]`, `y=0` | [x] |\n63\t| 6  | `driver` | B=true: the exact `x==1 && y==4` special case (`goto label2`) | [x] |\n64\t| 7  | `driver` | B=false via `y!=4`: `x=1`, randomized `y ∈ [1,64]\\{4}` | [x] |\n65\t| 8  | `driver` | B=false via `x!=1`: randomized `x ∈ [0,64]\\{1}`, `y=4` | [x] |\n66\t| 9  | `driver` | E=`x<3` boundary: `x=2`, randomized `y ∈ [1,64]` | [x] |\n67\t| 10 | `driver` | E=`x>=3` boundary: `x=3`, randomized `y ∈ [1,64]` | [x] |\n68\t| 11 | `driver` | E flips mid-run: `x=4` (first decrement lands on 3), randomized `y ∈ [1,64]` | [x] |\n69\t| 12 | `driver` | A=`x>0&&y>0`, E mixed: randomized `x ∈ [5,40]`, `y ∈ [1,40]` — starts with `while` re-tests, switches to back-edge once `x<3` | [x] |\n70\t| 13 | `driver` | full pruned cross product: **exhaustive** `x ∈ [-4,24] × y ∈ [-4,24]` (minus `x>0&&y<0`) | [x] |\n71\t| 14 | `driver` | randomized `x,y ∈ [-64,64]` (minus `x>0&&y<0`), 2000 seeded cases | [x] |\n72\t| 15 | `driver` | medium magnitudes: randomized `x,y ∈ [0,1000]`, 200 seeded cases | [x] |\n73\t| 16 | `driver` | asymmetric shapes: `y ≫ x` (`x ∈ {0,1,2}`, `y ∈ {500,1000,4096}`) and `x ≫ y` (`x ∈ {500,1000,5000}`, `y ∈ {0,1,2}`) | [x] |\n74\t| 17 | `driver` | large scale: `x ∈ {5_000, 50_000, 200_000} × y ∈ {0, 7, 200_000}` | [x] |\n75\t| 18 | `driver` | G: 100 sequential invocations and C/Rust interleaved invocations in one process (no hidden state / no cross-call contamination) | [x] |\n76\t| 19 | `driver` | F extremes with bounded runtime: `(INT_MIN, y>0)`, `(INT_MIN,0)`, `(INT_MIN,INT_MIN)`, `(-1,0)`, `(0,-1)`, `(0,0)`, `(1,0)`, `(0,1)` | [x] |\n77\t| 20 | `driver` | H: multi-MiB output forcing repeated `stdout` buffer flushes (`x=0,y=400_000`; `x=400_000,y=0`; `x=150_000,y=150_000`) | [x] |\n78\t\n79\t## Status\n80\t\n81\tAll 20 rows are implemented in `tests/differential.rs` and pass under every\n82\tfeature combination listed above (and additionally under `--release`).\n83\t\n84\t| row | test in `tests/differential.rs` | status |\n85\t|-----|----------------------------------|--------|\n86\t| 1 | `row01_loop_never_entered` | [x] |\n87\t| 2 | `row02_x_zero_small_y` | [x] |\n88\t| 3 | `row03_x_negative_y_positive` | [x] |\n89\t| 4 | `row04_y_zero_small_x` | [x] |\n90\t| 5 | `row05_y_zero_large_x` | [x] |\n91\t| 6 | `row06_special_case_x1_y4` | [x] |\n92\t| 7 | `row07_x1_y_not_4` | [x] |\n93\t| 8 | `row08_x_not_1_y4` | [x] |\n94\t| 9 | `row09_back_edge_boundary_x2` | [x] |\n95\t| 10 | `row10_back_edge_boundary_x3` | [x] |\n96\t| 11 | `row11_back_edge_flip_x4` | [x] |\n97\t| 12 | `row12_mixed_back_edge` | [x] |\n98\t| 13 | `row13_exhaustive_small_grid` | [x] |\n99\t| 14 | `row14_random_small` | [x] |\n100\t| 15 | `row15_random_medium` | [x] |\n101\t| 16 | `row16_asymmetric_shapes` | [x] |\n102\t| 17 | `row17_large_scale` | [x] |\n103\t| 18 | `row18_sequencing_and_interleaving` | [x] |\n104\t| 19 | `row19_extremes_bounded` | [x] |\n105\t| 20 | `row20_multi_mib_output` | [x] |\n106\t\n107\tRoughly 5 800 distinct `(x, y)` configurations are compared per run, each with\n108\tboth libraries invoked through their `.so` export.\n109\t\n110\t## How the comparison works\n111\t\n112\t`driver` is `void`-returning and communicates only through `stdout`, so the\n113\tobservable output is the byte stream on fd 1 **plus** the process termination\n114\tstatus. `tests/common/mod.rs` performs every call in a forked child whose fd 1\n115\tis a temporary file, then compares the bytes *and* the raw `waitpid` status of\n116\tthe C child against the Rust child. (A forked child is required: libtest keeps\n117\twriting its own progress lines to fd 1 from other threads, which would\n118\tcontaminate an in-process redirect.)\n119\t\n120\tNon-terminating inputs (`x > 0 && y < 0`, `x` near `INT_MAX`) are compared as a\n121\tbyte-capped prefix produced in a child that is `SIGKILL`ed once a full window\n122\thas been read — see `ERRORS.md` rows 14/15.\n123\t\n124\t## Reproducing\n125\t\n126\t```sh\n127\t./check_all.sh                     # every feature combination, symbols + tests\n128\tcargo build --offline              # NOTE: `cargo test` does not rebuild a cdylib\n129\tcargo test  --offline              # the harness refuses to run on a stale .so\n130\t```\n131\t\n132\tThe suite was validated by mutation testing: 8 independent mutations of\n133\t`src/lib.rs` (`y == 4`→`y == 5`, `x < 3`→`x <= 3`, `y == 0`→`y <= 0`,\n134\t`x > 0`→`x >= 0`, `||`→`&&`, `goto label2`→`goto label1`, `x--`→`x -= 2`,\n135\t`\"loop\\n\"`→`\"Loop\\n\"`) were each detected by at least one failing test.\n136\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01G2LmWbTZtBMi7QzWiNqPwm","session_id":"eeb44132-fb7e-4437-9dd9-10fc85cd1842","uuid":"ae47236d-7831-4243-9f5f-238a5b030feb","timestamp":"2026-08-18T04:05:31.956Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Audit C vs Rust for divergence"}
