{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01RSeodGqrJ11dDqMCPr9aN5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# SYMBOLS.md — Phase A: exported-symbol surface\n2\t\n3\tMechanically derived from `nm -D` on both shared objects.\n4\t\n5\t## Build commands\n6\t\n7\t```sh\n8\t# C shared library\n9\tcd translated_rust/c_src && mkdir -p build && cd build && \\\n10\t  cmake .. -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON && cmake --build .\n11\t# -> c_src/build/libdriver.so\n12\t\n13\t# Rust shared library (crate-type = [\"cdylib\"])\n14\tcd translated_rust && cargo build --offline\n15\t# -> target/debug/libdriver.so\n16\t```\n17\t\n18\t## C source inventory (completeness check)\n19\t\n20\tEvery non-build file under `c_src/`:\n21\t\n22\t| file | translated to | status |\n23\t|------|---------------|--------|\n24\t| `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` | (build system, no options/`#define`s) | n/a |\n25\t| `c_src/include/driver.h` | declaration of `driver` | covered |\n26\t| `c_src/src/driver.c` | `src/lib.rs` (`driver`) | fully translated |\n27\t\n28\t`c_src` contains exactly one translation unit and one public declaration, so no\n29\tC module was skipped (`find c_src -type f | grep -v build/` → 3 files above).\n30\t\n31\t## `nm -D --defined-only` — C `.so`\n32\t\n33\t```\n34\t0000000000001109 T driver\n35\t```\n36\t\n37\t## `nm -D --defined-only` — Rust `.so`\n38\t\n39\t```\n40\t00000000000122a0 T driver\n41\t```\n42\t\n43\t## Symbol parity table\n44\t\n45\t| # | symbol | C `.so` | Rust `.so` | notes |\n46\t|---|--------|---------|-----------|-------|\n47\t| 1 | `driver` | `T` | `T` | `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub extern \"C\" fn driver(c_int, c_int)` |\n48\t\n49\t**Missing from Rust `.so`: none. Symbol diff is EMPTY.**\n50\t\n51\t## Undefined (imported) symbols\n52\t\n53\tBoth libraries import only libc / runtime symbols, no cross-library\n54\tdependencies:\n55\t\n56\t* C `.so` imports: `puts@GLIBC_2.2.5` (gcc turns `printf(\"loop\\n\")` into\n57\t  `puts(\"loop\")`), plus the usual weak `_ITM_*`, `__cxa_finalize`,\n58\t  `__gmon_start__`.\n59\t* Rust `.so` imports: `printf@GLIBC_2.2.5` and the standard Rust-std/libgcc\n60\t  set (`_Unwind_*`, `malloc`, `memcpy`, `pthread_*`, …). All are libc /\n61\t  unwinder symbols; **0 missing/undefined non-libc symbols**.\n62\t\n63\t`puts(\"loop\")` vs `printf(\"%s\", \"loop\\n\")` emit the identical byte stream\n64\t(`loop\\n`) through the same `stdout` `FILE`, so the observable output is\n65\tbyte-identical — verified by the differential tests.\n66\t\n67\t## Verification script\n68\t\n69\t`./check_all.sh` regenerates both `.so`s and re-diffs the symbol lists for\n70\tevery feature combination (see `CONFIGS.md` §Feature combinations). Result:\n71\t\n72\t```\n73\t=== [combo1] symbol parity ===   (--no-default-features)\n74\tOK: all 1 C symbol(s) exported by the Rust .so\n75\tOK: no non-libc undefined symbols\n76\t=== [combo2] symbol parity ===   (default)\n77\tOK: all 1 C symbol(s) exported by the Rust .so\n78\tOK: no non-libc undefined symbols\n79\t=== [combo3] symbol parity ===   (--all-features)\n80\tOK: all 1 C symbol(s) exported by the Rust .so\n81\tOK: no non-libc undefined symbols\n82\t```\n83\t\n84\t`target/release/libdriver.so` (profile with `panic = \"abort\"`) also exports\n85\t`driver` and passes the full suite.\n86\t\n87\tChecklist:\n88\t\n89\t* [x] `nm -D` shows 0 symbols missing from the Rust `.so` (`comm -23` diff empty).\n90\t* [x] `nm -D` shows 0 undefined non-libc symbols in the Rust `.so`.\n91\t* [x] No C source file was left untranslated (inventory above).\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01G2LmWbTZtBMi7QzWiNqPwm","session_id":"eeb44132-fb7e-4437-9dd9-10fc85cd1842","uuid":"c308c259-adc8-4686-b904-849cd6c3722a","timestamp":"2026-08-18T04:06:10.136Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Audit C vs Rust for divergence"}
